## What is Hashing?

Hashing is a technique used to store and retrieve data in O(1) average time complexity.

A hash function converts a key into an index where the value is stored.

Example:

Key = "Jitu"

Hash Function

↓

Index = 7

↓

Store at bucket 7

---

## Map vs Unordered Map

| Feature | map | unordered_map |
|----------|------|------|
| Internal DS | Red Black Tree | Hash Table |
| Order | Sorted | Random |
| Insert | O(log n) | O(1) avg |
| Search | O(log n) | O(1) avg |
| Delete | O(log n) | O(1) avg |

